<phyphox version="1.20" locale="en">
  <title>Probe 5: the torch can strobe</title>
  <category>Probes</category>
  <description>
        Diagnostic. Takes ten seconds and tells you one thing: whether the flashlight output exists, which only the Strobe Tacho needs

        Run the probes in order. The FIRST one that fails to import, or shows nothing, names the feature your phyphox version will not do - which turns "none of it works and I have no idea why" into a single specific problem.
    
        NEEDS PHYPHOX 1.2.1 OR NEWER. The flashlight output arrives in that version, which is still in public beta - on 1.2.0 and earlier phyphox refuses the file with 'Unknown tag flashlight'. That is a version gap, not a fault.
    </description>

  <data-containers>
    <container size="64">raw</container>
    <container>probe</container>
    <container init="4">hz</container>
    <container init="1">bright</container>
    <container init="0.2">duty</container>
  </data-containers>

  <input>
    <sensor type="accelerometer" rate="0">
      <output component="abs">raw</output>
    </sensor>
  </input>
  <output>
    <flashlight>
      <input parameter="intensity">bright</input>
      <input parameter="frequency">hz</input>
      <input parameter="dutycycle">duty</input>
    </flashlight>
  </output>

  <views>
    <view label="Result">
      <info label="The torch should be flashing about four times a second while this runs. If it stays dark, your phyphox version has no flashlight output and only the Strobe Tacho is affected - everything else still works."/>
      <value label="Flash rate" unit="Hz" precision="0">
        <input>hz</input>
      </value>
      <value label="(this number just proves the analysis ran)" precision="2">
        <input>probe</input>
      </value>
    </view>
  </views>
  <analysis sleep="0.5">
    <average>
      <input as="buffer" clear="false">raw</input>
      <output as="average">probe</output>
    </average>
  </analysis>

  <export>
    <set name="Probe">
      <data name="value">probe</data>
    </set>
  </export>
</phyphox>
